  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on which lottery is more right-skewed (i.e., assigns higher probability to unfavorable outcomes) and prefers the more right-skewed one (Lottery A). However, the individual prefers Lottery B because it offers a higher chance of winning something (50% vs 25%), which reflects a preference for reducing the chance of getting nothing — the opposite of favoring right-skewness. The individual values decreasing the probability of unfavorable outcomes, while the decision reason favors increasing it (by preferring more right-skewed lotteries). The information considered by the individual (chance of winning something) is related to the same underlying probabilities but interpreted in the inverse direction. The individual’s justification contradicts the rule of the decision reason. Therefore, it is certain that the individual did not use this decision reason; in fact, their reasoning opposes it.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
